  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Late rallies won't erase early fragility forever.",
    "what_this_means": "They held the lead through six innings. Atlanta clawed back to tie it in the second and third, and for a stretch it looked like the kind of game that slips away. But Machado's two home runs supplied the power the lineup needed, and Tatis's eighth-inning shot sealed it. Buehler pitched into the sixth without breaking, and the bullpen. Matsui, Rodriguez, Morejon, Miller. Didn't allow another run after he left. This was offensive depth meeting pitching depth at the right moment. The 13 hits and 8 runs announced something different: the lineup didn't just score, it sustained. They left runners on base again. 10 RISP at-bats, only 3 converted. But the ones they did convert mattered. This is the thin margin they're learning to live with, and it held today.",
    "what_to_watch": "Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez has a 3.54 ERA for Atlanta tonight, and King brings a 3.41 mark over his last four starts into a 4:15 PM first pitch.",
